{pad:meta title='Icons'/}

<p>{app:tag 'icon:star'/} writes an interface icon of PAD's own set - {pad:echo php:count(padIconNames())/} of
them, drawn on a 24 by 24 grid as lines in the colour of the text around it, written as inline SVG.
Beside text an icon is decoration that a screen reader skips; alone in a button or a link it gets
<code>label=</code> and is read out by that name.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/icons_1'/}

<h2>An icon is a file</h2>

<p>Every icon is a file of <code>pad/subs/icons/types/</code>, <code>&lt;name&gt;.svg</code> - a whole SVG
that a browser shows as it is - and the files there are the icons there are. The icon type writes one
by its name, <code>{pad:open/}icon:cloud-upload/{pad:close/}</code>; the names are never used alone, as they
are the names of fields and pages too. <code>size=</code> and <code>stroke=</code> are the size in
pixels and the width of the lines.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/icons_2'/}

<ul>
  <li><code>padIconNames ()</code> lists the icons for a page's PHP, and the showcase draws
  <a href="../showcase/?icon/gallery">every icon</a> by its name.</li>
  <li>Each icon has the classes <code>pad-icon pad-icon-&lt;name&gt;</code> for styling.</li>
  <li>A name that is no icon is an error under the strict check, which names the icons close to
  it.</li>
</ul>
